---
import BaseLayout from "../components/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — Erik Fryscok"
  description="Learn how Erik Fryscok approaches engineering leadership, AI-enabled development, documentation, developer experience, and sustainable software delivery."
>
  <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6">About</h1>

    <!-- Professional Narrative -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Background</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
        I'm a software development team lead focused on helping engineering teams
        build better software. My work sits at the intersection of engineering
        leadership, modern infrastructure, and practical AI adoption.
      </p>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
        Over the years, I've worked across the full lifecycle of software delivery —
        from architecture and cloud infrastructure to developer tooling, documentation,
        and team culture. What ties it all together is a belief that the best outcomes
        come from investing in the systems and practices that help teams work more
        effectively.
      </p>
      <p class="text-gray-700">
        Today I'm focused on AI-enabled development, cloud infrastructure, and
        building engineering practices that scale with the team rather than against it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Engineering Philosophy -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Engineering Philosophy</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
        I believe software teams should work in ways that are sustainable, transparent,
        and grounded in practical reality. Here are the beliefs that shape how I
        approach engineering work:
      </p>
      <ul class="text-gray-700 space-y-3 list-disc list-inside">
        <li>
          <strong>AI-enablement over automation for its own sake.</strong> AI tools
          should augment team judgment and reduce friction, not replace the thinking
          that makes software reliable.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Documentation as a first-class artifact.</strong> Good documentation
          is not a side project — it's the difference between knowledge trapped in
          one person's head and knowledge the whole team can build on.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Practical systems over theoretical purity.</strong> The best architecture
          is one the team can maintain, evolve, and explain to a new hire on day one.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Developer experience is a team multiplier.</strong> Investing in tooling,
          onboarding, and local development environments pays compounding returns across
          every project and every new team member.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Leadership Approach -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Leadership Approach</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
        Leading engineering teams is about creating conditions where good work happens.
        My approach centers on three themes:
      </p>
      <ul class="text-gray-700 space-y-3 list-disc list-inside">
        <li>
          <strong>Mentoring and growth.</strong> I invest in helping team members develop
          the skills and confidence to take on increasingly complex work. The measure of
          good leadership is a team that doesn't need you.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Engineering culture.</strong> Culture isn't perks — it's the daily
          practices around code review, incident response, documentation, and how we
          treat each other when things go wrong. I lead by example in those moments.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Driving outcomes, not activity.</strong> Busy teams are not necessarily
          effective teams. I focus on clear goals, measurable progress, and removing
          the obstacles that slow delivery.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Interests -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Interests</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
        The areas I focus on most and enjoy writing about:
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
        <span class="px-3 py-1 bg-gray-100 text-gray-700 rounded-full text-sm">AI-enabled development</span>
        <span class="px-3 py-1 bg-gray-100 text-gray-700 rounded-full text-sm">Cloud infrastructure</span>
        <span class="px-3 py-1 bg-gray-100 text-gray-700 rounded-full text-sm">DevOps and CI/CD</span>
        <span class="px-3 py-1 bg-gray-100 text-gray-700 rounded-full text-sm">Documentation and knowledge management</span>
        <span class="px-3 py-1 bg-gray-100 text-gray-700 rounded-full text-sm">Developer productivity</span>
        <span class="px-3 py-1 bg-gray-100 text-gray-700 rounded-full text-sm">Engineering leadership</span>
        <span class="px-3 py-1 bg-gray-100 text-gray-700 rounded-full text-sm">Local AI and open-weight models</span>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
